nic","0.91% saline","concentrated brine","absolute ethanol"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"Water rushes in because $\\pi$ outside is far smaller than $\\pi$ of the cytoplasm (haemolysis).","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"medium","concept_id":"osmotic-pressure","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-258","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"At 273 K a solution with C = 0.50 mol L⁻¹ (R = 0.0821 L atm K⁻¹ mol⁻¹) has osmotic pressure nearest","options":["11.2 atm","0.50 atm","22.4 atm","1.00 atm"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"$\\pi = 0.50 \\times 0.0821 \\times 273 \\approx 11.2$ atm.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"medium","concept_id":"osmotic-pressure","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-259","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"Urea 3.0 g (60 g mol⁻¹) occupies 250 mL of solution at 27 °C. Using R = 0.0821 L atm K⁻¹ mol⁻¹, $\\pi$ is nearest","options":["4.9 atm","2.5 atm","0.82 atm","12 atm"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"C = 0.050 / 0.250 = 0.20 M; T = 300 K; $\\pi = 0.20 \\times 0.0821 \\times 300 \\approx 4.9$ atm.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"hard","concept_id":"osmotic-pressure","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-260","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"An aqueous NaCl solution that is 0.10 M and fully ionised (i = 2) at 300 K (R = 0.0821 L atm K⁻¹ mol⁻¹) has $\\pi$ nearest","options":["4.93 atm","2.46 atm","0.20 atm","8.21 atm"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"$\\pi = iCRT = 2 \\times 0.10 \\times 0.0821 \\times 300 = 4.93$ atm.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"hard","concept_id":"osmotic-pressure","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false}]$json$::jsonb) as x(
